Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 07:39:11 +0000

This builds the hub that "[PATCH v2] jails/instances/lab-mail: Spec
the list's mail hub" [1] describes, now on b/dev. It turns the relay
jail into the list's home: OpenSMTPD takes posts, Dovecot holds and
serves the list, and mbsync keeps it in sync with Fastmail.

Patch 1 revises the spec on two points that turned up while building
it. LMTP alone files only into INBOX, so a Sieve script from Pigeonhole
puts each post into lists. And Dovecot answers OK to a reader's STORE
and EXPUNGE without changing anything, rather than refusing them, so
the rights section and acceptance step 7 now say so.

Patch 2 is the implementation.

What I tested, in a rootless Dovecot 2.3.21 run from the FreeBSD
packages the jail installs, with ports and paths moved under /tmp:
- OpenSMTPD's own mail.lmtp delivers a post into lists, with
  Return-Path and Delivered-To: lab-devel@p7x.dev added and nothing
  else changed.
- A reader login with any password gets rights "lr". SELECT opens
  lists read-only, STORE and EXPUNGE change nothing, and MOVE and
  APPEND answer NO.
- pat@p7x.dev and mbsync log in only with their imap-users password,
  in any case. Each gets "lrwstie", and Pat's MOVE to Archive works.
- The sync config against a maildir standing in for Fastmail: posts
  and Fastmail mail cross both ways, an archived message reaches
  Archive on the far side and is only marked \Deleted in its lists,
  and a quiet run logs nothing.
- The import of a jj maildir copy as Pat, as README.org gives it.
- check-message against fake filter sessions: a good message, no
  Message-ID, two From fields, a header with no empty line after it,
  an mbox "From " line, and a leading continuation line. Only the good
  message and a folded Subject pass.
- smtpd -n accepts smtpd.conf, and doveconf -n accepts dovecot.conf.

What I could not test: smtpd itself needs root, so the recipient
sorting, the discard action, and the filter wiring are checked only
for syntax. The same goes for the check script and the jail build.
Steps 1 to 6 and 11 to 13 of the acceptance test cover them.

The clients on beastie and lab-claude are not in this series. Moving
them to the hub retires the jj maildir that lab-process-mail runs on,
and the spec leaves its new loop to a spec of its own. So the hub can
be built and checked now while nothing else changes.

